<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central India Agency</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1854–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Agency was the British political agency that supervised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of central India, including Indore, Gwalior, Bhopal and many small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> and Baghelkhand states. An Agent to the Governor-General based at Indore oversaw subordinate agencies. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> its states acceded to India and were merged into Madhya Bharat, Vindhya Pradesh and other unions in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-india-agency.jpg" alt="Central India Agency" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PadFoot2008 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_India_Agency_in_the_Indian_Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
